QUESTION 3: Print Odd and Even Numbers Alternately?
==============================================================================

class NumberPrinter {

    private int number = 1;
    private final int limit = 10;

    public synchronized void printOdd() {
        while (number <= limit) {
            while (number % 2 == 0) {
                try {
                    wait();
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                    return;
                }
            }

            if (number <= limit) {
                System.out.println("Odd  : " + number++);
                notifyAll();
            }
        }
    }

    public synchronized void printEven() {
        while (number <= limit) {
            while (number % 2 != 0) {
                try {
                    wait();
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                    return;
                }
            }

            if (number <= limit) {
                System.out.println("Even : " + number++);
                notifyAll();
            }
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        NumberPrinter printer = new NumberPrinter();

        new Thread(printer::printOdd).start();
        new Thread(printer::printEven).start();
    }
}

Explanation: wait() releases the lock and pauses the wrong thread. notifyAll() wakes the other thread.

