QUESTION 59: Factory Pattern in Spring Boot?
==============================================================================

Factory Pattern centralizes object creation based on runtime selection.

interface PaymentProcessor {
    String type();
    void process();
}

@Component
class PaymentProcessorFactory {

    private final Map<String, PaymentProcessor> processors;

    PaymentProcessorFactory(List<PaymentProcessor> processorList) {
        this.processors = processorList.stream()
                .collect(Collectors.toMap(
                        PaymentProcessor::type,
                        Function.identity()
                ));
    }

    PaymentProcessor get(String type) {
        PaymentProcessor processor = processors.get(type);

        if (processor == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "Unsupported payment type: " + type
            );
        }
        return processor;
    }
}

It avoids large if-else or switch blocks.

