QUESTION 67: Two Instances Updating the Same DB Row?
==============================================================================

Use optimistic locking:

@Entity
class Account {

    @Id
    private Long id;

    @Version
    private Long version;

    private BigDecimal balance;
}

If two instances update the same version, one succeeds and the other receives an optimistic-lock failure.

For strict locking:

@Lock(LockModeType.PESSIMISTIC_WRITE)
@Query("select a from Account a where a.id = :id")
Optional<Account> findForUpdate(@Param("id") Long id);

Prefer optimistic locking when conflicts are uncommon.

